/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  pump03_generic_selection
  ========================

  CHOOSING A CENTRIFUGAL PUMP WITH NO CATALOGUE (DEV.md 4c C441, level 1).
  Water at 25 degC, 50 m3/h, from a tank at 1.2 bar absolute (liquid 1 m
  above the pump axis, 0.8 m of suction-line loss) to a header at 7 bar.
  The shaft power is NOT typed with an efficiency: the pump asks Gulich's
  statistics what efficiency a well-designed single-stage radial pump of
  this duty has, and the run prints every number it estimated.

  Source of EVERY correlation: Gulich, Centrifugal Pumps, 4th ed.,
  Springer 2020.  Pages are printed in the run beside each number.
      specific speed   nq = n sqrt(Q) / H^0.75            Eq. T3.4.15, p. 154
      efficiency       eta_opt(Q, nq)                      Eq. T3.9.1,  p. 163
                       uncertainty +- 0.2 (1 - eta_opt)    Eq. T3.9.10, p. 163
      NPSH3 (BEP)      nss = n sqrt(Q) / NPSH3^0.75        Eq. 6.7,     p. 320
                       nss from the impeller class         Table D6.1,  p. 320
      NPSH available   (P_in - p_v)/(rho g) + z_e + ...    Eq. T2.2.8,  p. 52
      margin           NPSHA >= max(1.25 NPSH3, NPSH3+0.6) Table 6.2,   p. 379
      preferred range  0.85 < Q/Qbep < 1.1                 Sect. 10.9,  p. 806

  WHAT TO READ IN THE RUN.  The "Pump selection" block: nq (about 16, a low
  specific speed, a narrow radial impeller), the efficiency Gulich expects
  and its band, the NPSH3 the suction specific speed implies, the NPSHA the
  flowsheet computes from the inlet stream, the margin against the Table 6.2
  minimum, and whether the duty lies in the preferred operation range.
  Every one is marked `estimated`: they are statistics of many pumps, with
  the band Gulich gives, not a promise of any maker.

  Hand check (nq): n = 2900 rpm, Q = 50/3600 = 0.01389 m3/s,
  H = dP/(rho g) = 5.8e5/(997*9.80665) = 59.3 m ->
  nq = 2900*sqrt(0.01389)/59.3^0.75 = 2900*0.1179/21.4 = 16.0.

  WHAT THE LEVEL IS NOT: it knows nothing of a particular pump, of the
  part-load or overload efficiency (the BEP value is used and said so), of
  viscosity, or of the impeller's tip speed (the NPSHA rule of Table 6.2
  that depends on u1 is not asked, only its minimum).  Use level 2 (case
  pump04_manufacturer_curve) when a maker's curve exists.

  The standards that fix the margins and the preferred regions (the Hydraulic
  Institute's, API 610 / ISO 13709, ISO 9906 for curve tolerances) are cited
  for WHAT they rule; their numbers are not in Choupo until a copy is in the
  project's folder.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

// stream state lives on disk in 0/ (per-stream files); flowsheetDict is TOPOLOGY only

units
(
    {
        name        pump03;
        type        pump;
        in          feed;
        outputs     ( out );

        operation
        {
            P_out       7 bar;               // the header the pump must reach
            efficiency  estimated;           // Gulich Eq. T3.9.1, NOT a typed number

            selection
            {
                speed       2900 rpm;        // a 2-pole motor at 50 Hz
                impeller    standardAxialInlet;   // Table D6.1: nss 160 to 220, the lower limit
            }

            suction
            {
                staticHead  1 m;             // z_e: the liquid level above the pump axis
                lineLoss    0.8 m;           // H_v,s: loss in the suction line
            }
        }
    }
);
